==Irish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Ulster}} {{IPA|ga|/fˠaː/|qual2=unstressed|/fˠa/}}

===Preposition===
{{ga-prep|d|l}}

# {{alternative form of|ga|faoi||about, concerning|from=Ulster}}

====Usage notes====
The standard Irish and Connacht form {{m|ga|faoi}} (Munster {{m|ga|fé}}) means both ‘under’ and ‘about, concerning’. In Ulster, these two meanings are split: {{m|ga|faoi}} means ‘under’, while {{m|ga||fá}} means ‘about, concerning’.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ga|fád|pos=contraction with {{m|ga|do||your {{g|s}}}}}}
* {{l|ga|fám|pos=contraction with {{m|ga|mo||my}}}}
* {{l|ga|fán}} corresponding to standard {{l|ga|faoin}}
* {{l|ga|fána}} corresponding to standard {{l|ga|faoina}}
* {{l|ga|fánar}} corresponding to standard {{l|ga|faoinar}}
* {{l|ga|fánár}} corresponding to standard {{l|ga|faoinár}}
* {{l|ga|fánarb}} corresponding to standard {{l|ga|faoinarb}}
* {{l|ga|fánarbh}} corresponding to standard {{l|ga|faoinarbh}}

